§ `s 9-20 -- enterprise`

-- Jake rides as an independent contractor (k040), with a reasonable expectation of profit: a business, an enterprise.
#ASSERT `Am I carrying on an enterprise` `a delivery rider's business`
-- s 9-20(2)(c) excludes only individuals and partnerships of individuals; a company needs no expectation of profit.
#ASSERT `Am I carrying on an enterprise` `a company's business`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I carrying on an enterprise` `an employee's job`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I carrying on an enterprise` `a hobby`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I carrying on an enterprise` `an individual's activity with no expectation of profit`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I carrying on an enterprise` `a business not yet started`

§ `s 23-15 -- the threshold`

#ASSERT `What is my registration turnover threshold` FALSE 75000 EQUALS 75000
-- With no higher amount in the regulations, the Act's own figures: $50,000, or $100,000 for a non-profit body.
#ASSERT `What is my registration turnover threshold` FALSE 0 EQUALS 50000
#ASSERT `What is my registration turnover threshold` TRUE 0 EQUALS 100000

§ `ss 9-75, 188-30 -- value; Division 188 -- turnover`

-- s 9-75's own example: $22,000 -> value $20,000.
#ASSERT `What is the value of a taxable supply` 22000 EQUALS 20000
-- s 188-30: a supply that is not taxable counts at its full price: 11/10 of 10/11.
#ASSERT `What does a supply count for in my turnover` 31000 FALSE EQUALS 31000
#ASSERT `What is my current GST turnover` `Jake's takings, $31,000` FALSE EQUALS 31000
-- Registered: $82,500 GST-inclusive counts as $75,000.
#ASSERT `What is my current GST turnover` `$82,500 of supplies` TRUE EQUALS 75000
-- Registered with $55,000 taxable (value $50,000) and $30,000 GST-free (counts $30,000): $80,000.
#ASSERT `What is my current GST turnover` `$85,000 of which $30,000 GST-free` TRUE EQUALS 80000
-- s 188-15(1)(a), (3)(a): input taxed and offshore supplies are left out: $60,000.
#ASSERT `What is my current GST turnover` `$90,000 of which $30,000 input taxed or offshore` FALSE EQUALS 60000
-- s 188-25: a capital asset sale is left out of projected turnover (current turnover would count it).
#ASSERT `What is my projected GST turnover` `$100,000 of which $40,000 a capital asset sale` FALSE EQUALS 60000
-- s 188-10(1): (a) current at or above, unless the Commissioner is satisfied projected is below; (b) projected at or above.
#ASSERT `Does my GST turnover meet the threshold` 75000 0 FALSE 75000
#ASSERT NOT `Does my GST turnover meet the threshold` 80000 60000 TRUE 75000
#ASSERT `Does my GST turnover meet the threshold` 74999 80000 FALSE 75000

§ `s 144-5, s 195-1 -- taxi travel`

#ASSERT `Do I supply taxi travel` TRUE TRUE
-- Food on an e-bike: no passengers, no taxi or limousine.
#ASSERT NOT `Do I supply taxi travel` FALSE FALSE

§ `jake k043 -- first tax return as a sole trader, $31,000`

-- An enterprise, turnover $31,000 current and projected, under $75,000; delivering food is not taxi travel (s 195-1:
-- "transporting passengers, by taxi or limousine"), so s 144-5 does not reach him. Not required; he may register (s 23-10(1)).
#ASSERT `Must I register for GST` `Jake, sole trader, 2028 (k043)` EQUALS `Not required, but I may register`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I required to be registered` `Jake, sole trader, 2028 (k043)`
-- Neither registered nor required, so his deliveries are not taxable supplies (s 9-5(d)): no GST, no return, no credit.
#ASSERT NOT `Is my supply a taxable supply` `Jake's deliveries, $31,000` FALSE
#ASSERT `How much GST must I pay on my supply` `Jake's deliveries, $31,000` FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT NOT `Must I lodge a GST return` FALSE
#ASSERT `How much input tax credit do I get` `Jake's $2,200 e-bike` FALSE EQUALS 0
-- Had he driven a taxi, s 144-5 would require registration on the same $31,000.
#ASSERT `Must I register for GST` `Jake, if he drove a taxi` EQUALS `Required to be registered: I supply taxi travel`
-- Carrying passengers in a car that is not a taxi or limousine is not taxi travel; whether a ride-sourcing car is a
-- "taxi" the Act does not say, so the answer turns wholly on that fact.
#ASSERT `Must I register for GST` `a ride-sourcing driver whose car is not a taxi or limousine` EQUALS `Not required, but I may register`

§ `daniel d049 -- Jarrah's GST turnover reaches $75,000`

-- Current $75,000 is "at or above" $75,000 (s 188-10(1)(a)); projected $90,000 is too ((b)). Required (s 23-5).
#ASSERT `Must I register for GST` `Jarrah, October 2032 (d049)` EQUALS `Required to be registered: my GST turnover meets the threshold`
#ASSERT `Must I apply to register now` `Jarrah, October 2032 (d049)`
-- s 25-1: within 21 days after 1 October 2032: 22 October 2032.
#ASSERT `By when must I apply to register` (Date 1 10 2032) EQUALS (Date 22 10 2032)
-- Registered, Jarrah sells an $11,000 licence: GST $1,000; buys a $3,300 laptop: credit $300; net amount $700.
#ASSERT `Is my supply a taxable supply` `a $11,000 software licence sold by Jarrah` TRUE
#ASSERT `How much GST must I pay on my supply` `a $11,000 software licence sold by Jarrah` TRUE EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `Is my purchase a creditable acquisition` `Jarrah's $3,300 laptop` TRUE
#ASSERT `How much input tax credit do I get` `Jarrah's $3,300 laptop` TRUE EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `What is my net amount` 1000 300 EQUALS 700
-- Its first full quarter ends 31 December 2032: return and payment by 28 February 2033 (ss 31-8, 33-3).
#ASSERT `By when must I lodge my quarterly return` `the quarter ending 31 December` 2032 EQUALS (Date 28 2 2033)

§ `ss 23-5, 23-10 -- other cases`

#ASSERT `Must I register for GST` `a business past $75,000 that the Commissioner accepts will fall back` EQUALS `Not required, but I may register`
#ASSERT `Must I register for GST` `a business below $75,000 that expects more` EQUALS `Required to be registered: my GST turnover meets the threshold`
#ASSERT `Must I register for GST` `a non-profit body at $80,000` EQUALS `Not required, but I may register`
#ASSERT `Must I register for GST` `a hobbyist selling $80,000` EQUALS `Not required, and not entitled to register: I carry on no enterprise`
#ASSERT `Must I register for GST` `someone about to start a business` EQUALS `Not required, and I may register from the date I intend to start`
#ASSERT `Must I register for GST` `an employee` EQUALS `Not required, and not entitled to register: I carry on no enterprise`
-- The same $77,000 of takings: registered, it counts as $70,000 and is under; unregistered, $77,000 and is over.
#ASSERT `Must I register for GST` `a registered business with $77,000 of takings` EQUALS `Not required, but I may register`
#ASSERT `Must I register for GST` `an unregistered business with $77,000 of takings` EQUALS `Required to be registered: my GST turnover meets the threshold`
#ASSERT `Am I required to be registered` `a registered business with $82,500 of takings`
#ASSERT `Am I required to be registered` `a registered business with GST-free sales`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I required to be registered` `a business with input taxed or offshore supplies`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I required to be registered` `a business selling a capital asset`
-- Without a higher amount from the regulations, $60,000 meets the Act's $50,000.
#ASSERT `Am I required to be registered` `a business at $60,000 if the regulations set no higher amount`

§ `s 9-5, s 9-70 -- taxable supplies and GST`

#ASSERT `How much GST must I pay on my supply` `the s 9-75 example: a car sold for $22,000` TRUE EQUALS 2000
-- GST only on the taxable part: $660 x 10/11 x 10% = $60.
#ASSERT `How much GST must I pay on my supply` `a $1,100 sale of which $440 is GST-free` TRUE EQUALS 60
#ASSERT NOT `Is my supply a taxable supply` `a $5,500 service supplied offshore` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Is my supply a taxable supply` `a $2,000 wholly GST-free supply` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Is my supply a taxable supply` `a $500 gift of stock` TRUE

§ `Division 11 -- input tax credits`

-- s 11-30: $100 full credit x 60% = $60; $200 x 50% of the consideration = $100.
#ASSERT `How much input tax credit do I get` `a $1,100 phone used 60% for the business` TRUE EQUALS 60
#ASSERT NOT `Is my purchase a creditable acquisition` `a $1,100 purchase from an unregistered seller` TRUE
#ASSERT `How much input tax credit do I get` `a $2,200 machine whose price I share half` TRUE EQUALS 100
#ASSERT NOT `Is my purchase a creditable acquisition` `a $440 private purchase` TRUE
-- s 29-80: a $55 purchase (value $50) needs no tax invoice; a $56 one does.
#ASSERT `Can I claim the credit in this return` 55 FALSE 0
#ASSERT NOT `Can I claim the credit in this return` 56 FALSE 0
#ASSERT `Can I claim the credit in this return` 5600 TRUE 0
-- s 29-70(2): within 28 days of a request made on 10 January 2033: 7 February 2033.
#ASSERT `By when must I give a tax invoice` (Date 10 1 2033) EQUALS (Date 7 2 2033)
-- A negative net amount is a refund (s 7-15).
#ASSERT `What is my net amount` 200 500 EQUALS (0 MINUS 300)

§ `ss 31-5, 31-8, 31-10 -- returns`

#ASSERT `Must I lodge a GST return` TRUE
#ASSERT `By when must I lodge my quarterly return` `the quarter ending 30 September` 2032 EQUALS (Date 28 10 2032)
#ASSERT `By when must I lodge my monthly return` 12 2032 EQUALS (Date 21 1 2033)
